### Lab Test Filtering Examples

### 1. Basic search by name
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?name=lipid

### 2. Filter by price range (minPrice and maxPrice)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=100&maxPrice=500

### 3. Filter by minimum price only
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=200

### 4. Filter by maximum price only
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?maxPrice=1000

### 5. Filter by exact price (using both min and max with same value)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=500&maxPrice=500

### 6. Filter by date range (createdFrom and createdTo)
# Format: YYYY-MM-DD or ISO 8601
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?createdFrom=2024-01-01&createdTo=2024-12-31

### 7. Filter by createdFrom only (tests created after this date)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?createdFrom=2024-06-01

### 8. Filter by createdTo only (tests created before this date)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?createdTo=2024-12-31

### 9. Combine price and date filters
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&createdFrom=2024-01-01&createdTo=2024-12-31

### 10. Filter by category and price
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?categoryId=YOUR_CATEGORY_ID&minPrice=200&maxPrice=800

### 11. Filter by active status and price
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?isActive=true&minPrice=100&maxPrice=500

### 12. Search with pagination and price filter
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?search=blood&page=1&limit=10&minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000

### 13. Filter by description
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?description=cholesterol

### 14. Combine multiple filters
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?name=lipid&minPrice=200&maxPrice=800&isActive=true&createdFrom=2024-01-01

### 15. Sort by price ascending with filters
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&sortBy=price&sortOrder=asc

### 16. Sort by price descending with filters
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&sortBy=price&sortOrder=desc

### 17. Sort by creation date ascending
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=asc

### 18. Sort by creation date descending (default)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc

### 19. Sort by name with price filter
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?minPrice=100&sortBy=name&sortOrder=asc

### 20. Complex query: Search, filter by price, date, status, and sort
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?search=test&minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&createdFrom=2024-01-01&createdTo=2024-12-31&isActive=true&sortBy=price&sortOrder=asc&page=1&limit=20

### 21. Filter by status (alternative to isActive)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?status=active

### 22. Filter inactive tests
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?status=inactive

### 23. Using ISO 8601 date format with time
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?createdFrom=2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z&createdTo=2024-12-31T23:59:59.999Z

### 24. Get all tests with pagination
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?page=1&limit=10

### 25. Get tests from specific category with price range
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/lab-tests?categoryId=YOUR_CATEGORY_ID&minPrice=500&maxPrice=2000&sortBy=price&sortOrder=asc

###
### Query Parameter Reference:
###
### Filtering:
### - name: string (partial match, case-insensitive)
### - description: string (partial match, case-insensitive)
### - search: string (searches both name and description)
### - categoryId: string (exact match)
### - isActive: boolean (true/false)
### - status: string ('active' or 'inactive')
### - minPrice: number (minimum price, inclusive)
### - maxPrice: number (maximum price, inclusive)
### - createdFrom: string (ISO date, tests created on or after this date)
### - createdTo: string (ISO date, tests created on or before this date)
###
### Pagination:
### - page: number (default: 1)
### - limit: number (default: 10)
###
### Sorting:
### - sortBy: string (field to sort by: 'name', 'price', 'createdAt', etc.)
### - sortOrder: string ('asc' or 'desc', default: 'desc')
###